    {
      "title": "Same-Origin Policy Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Same-Origin Policy Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What an Origin Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "**Origin** = ==scheme + host + port==; all three must match exactly."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Compared with https://a.com",
                "Same origin?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`http://a.com`",
                  "{red:No}: scheme"
                ],
                [
                  "`https://a.com:8443`",
                  "{red:No}: port"
                ],
                [
                  "`https://b.a.com`",
                  "{red:No}: host"
                ],
                [
                  "`https://a.com/page`",
                  "{green:Yes}: path ignored"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What SOP Blocks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "evil.com script",
                    "sub": "calls fetch",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Request sent",
                    "sub": "simple request",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server replies",
                    "sub": "response returns",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Read blocked",
                    "sub": "JS sees nothing",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cross-origin action",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Embed `img`, `script`, `link`",
                  "{green:Allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "Submit a form POST",
                  "{green:Allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "Display an `iframe`",
                  "{green:Allowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "JS reads the contents",
                  "{red:Blocked}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. SOP vs CORS",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==SOP== = browser default, {red:restricts} reads",
                "==CORS== = opt-in server headers, {green:relaxes} reads",
                "Neither protects the server from `curl` or direct clients"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**What is an origin?** Scheme + host + port; all three must match.",
                "**Does SOP stop a request being sent?** No, only the read; a preflighted fetch stops at OPTIONS.",
                "**Why does a form POST work?** It is a send, not a read; the attacker never reads the reply."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CSRF Attacks and CSRF Tokens",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CSRF Attacks and CSRF Tokens",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What CSRF Is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Browser ==auto-attaches cookies== to a forged cross-site request",
                "Server sees an authenticated, state-changing action",
                "Attacker ==never reads== the response"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Needs all three: {red:cookie auth}, {red:state-changing endpoint}, {red:predictable params}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Token Defences",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Synchronizer",
                "Double-submit"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Token kept",
                  "Server, per session",
                  "Cookie plus request copy"
                ],
                [
                  "Sent in",
                  "Hidden field or header",
                  "Header or body"
                ],
                [
                  "Check",
                  "Matches stored token",
                  "Cookie equals copy"
                ],
                [
                  "Attacker fails",
                  "SOP: cannot read token",
                  "Cannot read cookie"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sign or ==HMAC== the double-submit token: stops subdomain cookie injection"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does a token defeat CSRF?** Attacker cannot read it (SOP), so cannot forge it",
                "**Why must GET never change state?** Links and img tags send GET with cookies, no token",
                "**Cookie-auth JSON API safe?** No: cookies still attach, and forms can post JSON as text/plain"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A token works only because the attacker ==cannot read it==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SameSite Cookies and Defence in Depth",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SameSite Cookies and Defence in Depth",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Values",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Value",
                "Cross-site cookie sent",
                "Catch"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:Strict}",
                  "Never, even link clicks",
                  "Login lost on inbound links"
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:Lax}",
                  "Top-level GET navigation only",
                  "Not POST, iframe, fetch; Chromium default only; set it explicitly"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:None}",
                  "All requests",
                  "Needs `Secure`; CSRF exposure returns"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Set-Cookie: sid=1; SameSite=Lax; Secure; HttpOnly"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Site vs Origin",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==site== = scheme + eTLD+1; ignores port and subdomain",
                "`a.com` and `b.a.com`: same-site, different origins",
                "`http://a.com` vs `https://a.com`: cross-site",
                "{red:Compromised subdomain} can still attack"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Defence in depth",
              "text": "SameSite is a layer, not a replacement: keep ==CSRF tokens==, Origin checks, no state-changing GET."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Strict vs Lax, who loses login?** Strict: a user clicking a link from email lands logged out; Lax keeps it.",
                "**SameSite a full replacement?** No: None, subdomains and non-Chromium defaults remain.",
                "**Origin vs site?** Origin is scheme+host+port; site is scheme + eTLD+1."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CORS Headers and Preflight Requests",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CORS Headers and Preflight Requests",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Origin and Allow-Origin",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Browser sends `Origin`; server replies `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` with it or `*`",
                "Browser decides whether ==JS may read== the response",
                "{green:Simple} (GET, HEAD, form/text POST, no custom headers): no preflight"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Preflight",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Browser OPTIONS",
                "Server answer"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Access-Control-Request-Method`",
                  "`Access-Control-Allow-Methods`"
                ],
                [
                  "`Access-Control-Request-Headers`",
                  "`Access-Control-Allow-Headers`"
                ],
                [
                  "(none)",
                  "`Access-Control-Max-Age` caches it"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Triggers: ==custom header==, `PUT`/`DELETE`, `Content-Type: application/json`",
                "Real request waits for the `OPTIONS` approval"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Credentials",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "fetch(url, { credentials: 'include' })"
              ],
              "note": "client side"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Response needs `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`",
                "Allowed origin ==explicit==, never `*`",
                "Non-simple response headers need `Access-Control-Expose-Headers`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**When is a preflight sent?** Custom header, PUT/DELETE or JSON content type.",
                "**Why no `*` with credentials?** Browsers reject it; a named origin is required.",
                "**Does CORS stop CSRF?** No; it limits reads, and simple requests are still sent."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common CORS Misconfigurations",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common CORS Misconfigurations",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Reflected Origin",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Server copies `Origin` into ==Allow-Origin== plus `Allow-Credentials: true`",
                "Any site can then **read** logged-in responses"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Weak Origin Checks",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Check",
                "Bypassed by"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`endsWith('example.com')`",
                  "`evil-example.com`"
                ],
                [
                  "Substring match",
                  "`example.com.evil.com`"
                ],
                [
                  "Trusts `null`",
                  "Sandboxed iframe, `file://`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Caches and Safe Validation",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dynamic origin needs ==Vary: Origin==",
                "Without it, a cache serves one origin's headers to another"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const ok = new Set(['https://app.example.com']);",
                "if (ok.has(req.headers.origin)) {",
                "  res.set('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', req.headers.origin);",
                "  res.set('Vary', 'Origin');",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "exact match against an allowlist"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never",
              "text": "Reflect Origin, trust `null`, or pair `*` with credentials."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Exploit reflected origin?** Evil page fetches with `credentials:'include'` and reads the reply",
                "**Why no `*` with credentials?** Any site could read authenticated data",
                "**Validate safely?** Exact match against an allowlist, never suffix or substring"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: SOP, CSRF, SameSite, CORS",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: SOP, CSRF, SameSite, CORS",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Origin vs site",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Is",
                "Ignores"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Origin",
                  "scheme + host + port",
                  "nothing"
                ],
                [
                  "Site",
                  "scheme + eTLD+1",
                  "port, subdomain"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "SOP blocks ==reads==, not sends",
                "No protection from direct requests like `curl`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. CSRF defences and cookies",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "1. SameSite",
                    "sub": "Lax / Strict",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2. Token",
                    "sub": "state-changing requests",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "3. Origin/Referer",
                    "sub": "check it",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "4. No GET writes",
                    "sub": "GET stays safe",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Set-Cookie: sid=abc; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax"
              ],
              "note": "set SameSite explicitly"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Cookie flags",
              "items": [
                "`HttpOnly`: no JS access",
                "`Secure`: HTTPS only",
                "`Lax`: only Chromium defaults to it",
                "`None` only with `Secure`"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. CORS headers",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Access-Control-...",
                "Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Allow-Origin`",
                  "origin allowed to read"
                ],
                [
                  "`Allow-Methods`",
                  "preflight: methods"
                ],
                [
                  "`Allow-Headers`",
                  "preflight: request headers"
                ],
                [
                  "`Allow-Credentials`",
                  "`true`, explicit origin"
                ],
                [
                  "`Expose-Headers`",
                  "non-simple response headers"
                ],
                [
                  "`Max-Age`",
                  "cache the preflight"
                ],
                [
                  "`Vary: Origin`",
                  "when origin is dynamic"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Debug rule",
              "text": "A CORS error is the browser blocking the ==read==. Check response headers and the `OPTIONS` preflight status in DevTools. Never reflect `Origin`, trust `null`, or pair `*` with credentials."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A server copies the request Origin into Access-Control-Allow-Origin and sends Allow-Credentials: true. What can evil.com do?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Its JS calls fetch with credentials:'include' and **reads** the victim's logged-in responses",
                "Fix: exact allowlist match, plus Vary: Origin"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Cookie is SameSite=Lax. Which is still sent from evil.com: a form POST to /transfer, or a link click to GET /transfer?to=x?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The link click: Lax sends cookies on cross-site top-level GET navigations",
                "The POST is blocked, so state changes on GET stay exploitable"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Page on a.com fetches api.a.com with Content-Type: application/json. Is a preflight sent?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Yes: different origin, and JSON is not a simple content type",
                "If OPTIONS lacks Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, the real request is never sent"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}